<title>USA: Total CME July volume falls 7.8 pct year-on-year.</title>
<headline>Total CME July volume falls 7.8 pct year-on-year.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Chicago Mercantile Exchange (CME) reported that volume in its futures and options totaled 15,751,689 contracts in July, down 7.8 percent from 17,091,298 contracts a year earlier.</p>
<p>Open interest at the end of the month stood at 7,265,240 positions, up 10.7 percent from year-ago levels. The CME open interest record was set June 12 at 7,735,497, the exchange said.</p>
<p>Year-to-date volume through July totaled 127,194,021 contracts, up 5.8 percent from 120,186,548 during the same period in 1996.  </p>
<p>Major categories and volumes were as follows:</p>
<p>Futures (individual)   July 1997    % change	  July 1996</p>
<p>  Eurodollar	     7,631,612	 -16.6	  9,154,180</p>
<p>  Deutschemark	     521,405	 +14.5	    455,554</p>
<p>  Japanese yen	     409,047	 -11.4	    461,813</p>
<p>  Swiss franc		305,510	 -11.6	    345,546</p>
<p>  British pound	    264,929	 +22.2	    216,712</p>
<p>  Canadian dollar	  136,608	 +10.5	    123,604</p>
<p>  S&amp;P 500		  1,285,806	 -20.0	  1,607,739</p>
<p>  Live cattle		372,793	 +16.5	    320,114</p>
<p>  Lean hogs		  175,780     +1891.6		8,826</p>
<p>Options on futures</p>
<p>  Eurodollar	   2,074,408	  +27.3	   1,629,321</p>
<p>  Eurodollar midcurve  594,361	 +107.7	     286,145</p>
<p>  Deutschemark	   161,512	  -15.3	     190,738</p>
<p>  Japanese yen	   131,501	  -37.4	     210,032</p>
<p>  British pound	  184,723	  -66.3	     548,332</p>
<p>  S&amp;P 500		  441,058	   -6.8	     473,427</p>
<p>  Live cattle	     50,034	  +20.2		41,616</p>
<p>  Hogs			20,182	+2703.1		   720</p>
<p>Begining July 1, the CME no longer includes in its trading volume statistics transactions that the exchange has included since January 1994 including: deliveries, option exercises, futures positions established by the exercise of options, expired options and SIMEX mutual offset transactions cleared on the CME.</p>
